-- title:
--   p is a uniformiser at the minimal primes above p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 1$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that maps to $1$ under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Assume the Laurent series $j_q = q^{-1}\cdot(\text{integral power series } jNum)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ lies in the subfield $\mathbb{Q}(\,\text{ratios of integral }q\text{-expansions for } \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z}))$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Write $F$ for the corresponding subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ attached to $\Gamma_H(M)$ (the image in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$), $j \in F$ for the element $j_q$ there, and $R \subseteq \mathbb{Q}$ for the subring of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{inf}}$ be the subalgebras of $F$ of elements integral over $R[j]$, respectively over $R[j^{-1}]$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions: for every prime ideal $P$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ that is a minimal prime of the ideal generated by $p$, the image of that ideal in the localisation of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ at $P$ is the maximal ideal of that local ring; and likewise for $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{inf}}$.
--
--   This says that $p$ is a uniformiser at each point of codimension one above $p$ in the two affine charts of the integral model of $X_H(M)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ obtained by normalising $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$ and $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j^{-1}]$ in the $q$-expansion function field; classically it reflects the fact that, for $p \parallel M$, the branches of $X_H(M) \otimes \mathbb{F}_p$ over the generic point of the $j$-line are reduced. It is the input to the reducedness of the chart rings modulo $p$ for $\Gamma_H(M)$.
-- source:
